codemap 9
tour feature-registry
kind data
author ai
group cli
note The feature registry, crates/features: the one list of everything a user can do with codemap. Each Feature variant is one user function, and Feature::spec gives its Spec: the name (kebab-case, also the CLI command name), a one-line summary (the CLI help line or the GUI tooltip), the Surface it belongs to (Command for the CLI commands, which the GUI's console runs too, Window for what only the GUI does) and every Trigger that fires it: a command word, a key Chord, a click or typing on a named GUI element, or a Gesture on an element. The crate depends on nothing and holds no behaviour; the front ends build from it. The CLI's clap Command takes each command's name and help line from the spec, so help and the registry cannot disagree. The GUI binds keys and gestures by reading a feature's triggers (keys.rs), and names every clickable element through a Control that pairs a Feature with an Element (ids.rs), so a button or key that is not in the registry cannot be written, which xtask lint enforces for key bindings. Tests here check that names are unique, every feature has a trigger and a summary, a command feature is triggered by exactly its own name, and no trigger fires two features; the GUI's tests check that every Control's element is a trigger of its feature. Adding a user function starts here (the add-feature skill).

